                <head>No. 418<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>From July 10 to July 14, the Foreign Ministers of the United States, the United
                    Kingdom, and France met in Washington to discuss matters of mutual concern.
                    During the course of these meetings United States and United Kingdom officials
                    held several conversations <pb facs="1043" n="995" xml:id="pg995"/> on problems
                    affecting their interests alone. At the end of the meetings the three Foreign
                    Ministers approved the text of a note to the Soviet Union calling for a
                    four-power meeting on Germany and Austria. For documentation on the meetings of
                    the Foreign Ministers, see <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg_1582">volume V,
                        Part 2, pages 1582</ref> ff.</p>
            </div>
